# ============================================================================
# This repository is PRIVATE and DELIBERATELY contains live credentials:
#
#   ops/freellmapi.config.json   dashboard admin password + provider API keys
#   ops/secrets/                 ENCRYPTION_KEY + dashboard password backup
#   freellmapi/.env              ENCRYPTION_KEY (runtime env for the gateway)
#
# Stated plainly, so this decision is not a surprise later:
#
#   Git history is permanent. If this repository is ever made public, or a
#   collaborator is added, every one of those credentials is exposed, and
#   deleting the file afterwards does NOT undo it - the values have to be
#   ROTATED (new ENCRYPTION_KEY invalidates existing database backups; a new
#   unified API key invalidates every client).
#
#   Keep it private. Render supplies its own copies through its secret prompt;
#   these local files exist so the install is fully reproducible from a clone.
# ============================================================================

# ---- dependencies and build output: never belongs in Git ------------------
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

# ---- the upstream checkout's own git metadata -----------------------------
# freellmapi/ is a clone of a public project and has its own .git directory
# (26 MB). Its FILES are tracked here as ordinary files; its history is not.
freellmapi/.git/

# ---- live databases and backup blobs --------------------------------------
# Binary, constantly rewritten, and restorable from the encrypted backup that
# the gateway uploads. Push one deliberately if you ever need to.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.backup

# ---- local scratch output -------------------------------------------------
*.out
*.err
*.log

# ---- config backups -------------------------------------------------------
# Written by the add-a-key workflow before every edit. They duplicate every
# secret in the repo, so they are never committed.
ops/secrets/*.bak-*
